<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- RadarOverlayInput — how the RADAR LAYER ITSELF is drawn, as opposed to what is drawn over it. Reused in
     BOTH temporal windows (PastCast and NowCast), like StormReportsInput.

       Opacity ──────────────●──

     ⚠️ ONE SLIDER TODAY, and a whole control for it on purpose: this is the section every future setting
     that belongs to the radar LAYER goes in, and adding the second one should not mean inventing the
     section then. Its neighbours are the outlook's opacity and the reports' opacity — the radar's had no
     home at all until now.
     ⚠️ RadarOpacity was WIRED BUT UNREACHABLE before this: the property drives the map and has since the
     ribbon UI, but every generation of chrome since dropped its slider, so the value sat at its 0.85
     default with no way to change it. This is a re-add, not a new feature.

     ⚠️ THE VALUE IS GLOBAL — one map, one radar layer, one number, shared by live and replay. That is
     survivable in two windows only because PastCast and NowCast are MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE modes (Past clears
     Now, and MapViewModel closes the window of a mode that stops), so the two hosts can never both be on
     screen showing the same value. If that exclusivity ever changes, this becomes one control in two places
     disagreeing about which one you just moved.

     ⚠️ IT IS NOT GATED ON A LOADED WINDOW, unlike the outlook and storm-report controls beside it. Those
     were gated because they have nothing to FETCH without a convective day; opacity fetches nothing, so
     setting it before a load is harmless and lets you have the layer looking right when the frames arrive.

     ⚠️ THE SECTION HEADING IS NOT HERE — each host window draws its own, the same rule StormReportsInput
     follows. A window owns its section structure; this is content.

     Bound to RadarViewModel. -->
<UserControl x:Class="Anvil.Controls.Composites.RadarOverlayInput"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             mc:Ignorable="d">

    <Grid ColumnSpacing="12" VerticalAlignment="Top">
        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="60"/>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

        <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="Opacity" Style="{StaticResource SettingsFieldLabelStyle}"/>
        <Slider Grid.Column="1"
                HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                Minimum="0" Maximum="1"
                StepFrequency="0.05" SmallChange="0.05"
                IsThumbToolTipEnabled="False"
                VerticalAlignment="Center"
                Value="{x:Bind ViewModel.RadarOpacity, Mode=TwoWay}"
                ToolTipService.ToolTip="Opacity of the radar layer — turn it down to read an outlook through it"/>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
